From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:52:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 064/111] Two views: drag a tab to the other view's tab bar

A tab dragged from one view's tab bar onto a tab of the other view's bar
moves there, right after the tab it was dropped on, and is shown. Dragging
a tab within one view's bar reorders it. Both orders are those of all tabs,
so the session keeps them.

libcosmic's tab bar does not say which tab a drag carries. Only the bar a
drag started in reports drop hints, so the first hint names the dragged tab;
it is forgotten on a drop or the next press. A drop on a bar's empty space
does nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

